I am pretty sure that is not what you want. Agilent had microarrays 
called the G4110A and G4110B, and those are what the hgug4110a.db and 
hgug4110b.db are designed for.

I am not familiar with Agilent's website, and a cursory glance didn't 
result in me finding the annotation file for this array. But if you have 
such a thing (with say columns that contain the Agilent ID and another 
with Gene, UniGene, RefSeq, etc type IDs), then you can create your own 
pretty easily using the AnnotationDbi package.

Best,

Jim




